{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1146012-does-anyone-else-think-the-revised-edition-tradition-book-covers-are-cyberpunk","id":1146012,"title":"Does anyone else think the Revised edition Tradition Book covers are Cyberpunk?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-02T03:08:06-07:00","id":1146012,"title":"Does anyone else think the Revised edition Tradition Book covers are Cyberpunk?","content":"Everytime I look at Mage Revised and go to the art that is featured on the chapter breaks, the same art that adorns most but not all of the trad books, I can\u2019t help but to think it\u2019s very cyberpunk.<br /> <br /> Particularly, the Celestial Chorus, Akashic Brotherhood and Virtual Adept covers really invoke a cyberpunk feel to me. In fact, when I first looked at those pages over 15 years ago, they I actually thought that Mage was a Cyberpunk game.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d like to know if anyone felt similarly.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m curious to know how others feel, and felt, about the art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T11:43:32-07:00","id":1146113,"title":"","content":"They are. It was basically what Christopher Shy was into at the time. Before that, it was Celtic-style facial tattoos. And before that, it was something else, I forget what. It was an ongoing problem with his art, in that he'd constantly slap whatever his &quot;thing&quot; of the moment was onto character art, regardless of if it fit or not, and was also known to completely ignore art notes at times. So, you've got a bunch of revised edition Vampires with weird face tattoos (and one of the main Assamites, a clan who among other things get <i>darker</i> as they age, presented as an albino), and a bunch of Mage signature characters who all look like something out of William Gibson's work from the 1980s. I do remember that the chapter opening fiction in MageRev had to be heavily rewritten to fit the art (because it's faster to do that than vice versa). Also, I'm pretty sure that the person on the cover of the revised Verbena book was originally supposed to be African-American.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}